  '/': "<h1>Pet Waste Removal and Dog Poop Removal in Chattanooga, TN</h1><p>Scoopy Doo LLC is a locally owned pet waste removal and pooper scooper service based in Chattanooga, Tennessee, serving homes, HOAs, apartment communities, and commercial properties across the Chattanooga metro area and North Georgia. Scoopy Doo has 90 five-star reviews and more than 150 active clients, is accredited by the Better Business Bureau, and was featured by the Chattanoogan in June 2026 and by WDEF News 12 in July 2026. Scoopy Doo is also a member of aPaws, the Association of Professional Animal Waste Specialists. No contracts are required and service is available 7 days a week.</p><h2>What services does Scoopy Doo offer?</h2><p>Weekly dog poop removal is the most popular service. Scoopy Doo also offers twice-weekly service, every-other-week service, one-time yard cleanups, commercial pet waste removal for apartment complexes and businesses, and HOA common area cleanup. Scoopy Doo also installs dog doors and pet doors for homes in the same service area through Scoopy Doo Doggy Doors at scoopychatt.com/doggy-doors.</p><h2>How much does dog poop removal cost in Chattanooga?</h2><p>Weekly service starts at $20 per visit for one dog. Twice-weekly service is $18 per visit and every-other-week service starts at $33 per visit, each plus a small charge per additional dog. One-time yard cleanups start at $85, and optional waste takeaway is $5 per visit. Every quote is free and personalized to your yard size and number of dogs at scoopychatt.com/quoterequest. There are no contracts and no cancellation fees.</p><h2>What happens on every visit?</h2><p>You receive a text when your technician is on the way, so you do not need to be home. The technician searches the entire yard in a grid pattern, double-bags all waste, and places it in your outdoor bin, never at the gate; haul-away off the property is $5 per visit. After every visit your gate is secured and a photo confirmation is sent to your phone. Tools are sanitized between every yard.</p><h2>What areas does Scoopy Doo serve?</h2><p>In Tennessee: Chattanooga, Hixson, Red Bank, Signal Mountain, Lookout Mountain, Soddy-Daisy, Ooltewah, East Brainerd, East Ridge, Collegedale, Apison, Highland Park, and Downtown Chattanooga. In North Georgia: Ringgold, Rossville, Fort Oglethorpe, and Flintstone. North Georgia customers pay the same rates as Tennessee locations, with no extra fee for crossing the state line.</p><h2>How quickly can service start?</h2><p>Most new customers start within 2 to 5 days of requesting a quote, and Scoopy Doo responds the same day. Request a free quote at scoopychatt.com/quoterequest, email info@scoopychatt.com, or call 423-600-5040.</p>",
  '/dog-poop-removal-chattanooga': "<h1>Dog Poop Removal in Chattanooga, TN</h1><p>Scoopy Doo LLC provides professional dog poop removal for homes across Chattanooga, Tennessee and North Georgia. Service is available weekly, twice weekly, every other week, or as a single one-time cleanup, and no contract is required at any frequency.</p><h2>How much does dog poop removal cost in Chattanooga?</h2><p>Weekly service starts at $20 per visit for one dog. Twice-weekly service is $18 per visit and every-other-week service starts at $33 per visit, each plus a small charge for additional dogs. Quotes are free and based on your yard size and dog count at scoopychatt.com/quoterequest.</p><h2>How often should dog waste be removed?</h2><p>Weekly removal is the standard for households with one or two dogs. It keeps waste from accumulating, protects the lawn from nitrogen burn, and reduces the bacteria and parasites that build up in a yard between cleanings. Smaller yards and single-dog homes often do well on an every-other-week schedule.</p><h2>Is Scoopy Doo insured?</h2><p>Yes. Scoopy Doo LLC is fully insured on every visit, is accredited by the Better Business Bureau, and holds 90 five-star reviews across more than 150 active clients in the Chattanooga area. Call 423-600-5040 or email info@scoopychatt.com.</p>",
