  '/dog-poop-scooping-chattanooga': "<h1>Dog Poop Scooping Service in Chattanooga, TN</h1><p>Scoopy Doo LLC is a locally owned pooper scooper service in Chattanooga, Tennessee, serving the metro area and North Georgia 7 days a week. Scoopy Doo is not a national franchise. It is a family-run local business with 90 five-star reviews and more than 150 active clients.</p><h2>What happens during a scooping visit?</h2><p>You receive a text when the technician is on the way, so there is no need to be home as long as the gate is accessible. The technician walks the yard in a grid pattern so no section is missed, double-bags all waste, and removes it from the property. The gate is secured and photographed, and that photo is sent to your phone.</p><h2>Do you sanitize equipment between yards?</h2><p>Yes. Scooping tools are sanitized between every yard to avoid carrying bacteria or parasites from one property to the next.</p><h2>How do I start pooper scooper service?</h2><p>Request a free quote at scoopychatt.com/quoterequest. Scoopy Doo replies the same day and most new customers are on a route within 2 to 5 days. There are no contracts and no cancellation fees.</p>",
  '/yard-cleanup-chattanooga': "<h1>Yard Cleanup for Pet Owners in Chattanooga, TN</h1><p>Scoopy Doo LLC clears accumulated dog waste from Chattanooga and North Georgia yards in a single deep-clean visit. One-time cleanups suit spring cleaning, an overgrown yard after winter, preparing for a party, a move-out, or listing a home for sale.</p><h2>How much does a one-time yard cleanup cost?</h2><p>One-time cleanups start at $85, priced by yard size and how much waste has built up. Many customers book a one-time cleanup to reset the yard, then move onto weekly or every-other-week service from $20 per visit.</p><h2>What if the yard has not been cleaned in months?</h2><p>That is the normal case for a one-time cleanup. The technician grid-searches the entire yard, including wooded sections, tree lines, and areas under shrubs where waste is easy to miss. Everything is double-bagged and placed in your outdoor bin, never left at the curb. Haul-away off the property is $5 per visit.</p><h2>Why does built-up dog waste matter?</h2><p>Waste left on a lawn burns grass and damages soil, and it carries bacteria and parasites such as hookworms, roundworms, and giardia that persist in the yard. In heavy rain it washes into Chattanooga area waterways. Book a cleanup at scoopychatt.com/quoterequest or call 423-600-5040.</p>"
